WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.801
-We love our audience.
You watch us every night,

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:05.200
but right now we want to change
things up and watch you.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.567
We asked you guys at home

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:09.200
to send us some fun or unique
talents that you have.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.234
We got submissions
from thousands of people

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:12.534
all across the world.

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:13.868
And we're going to meet
some of them right now.

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:16.400
It's time for
"Show Me Something Good."

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.767
♪ -Show me something good ♪

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:22.868
♪ Show me something good,
show me something good ♪

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.534
♪ Just show me ♪

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.834
-Alright.
Let's meet our first guest.

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:29.801
Hello. What is your name
and where are you from?

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:33.934
-Hey, Jimmy, I'm Jemima June and
I'm from Nashville, Tennessee.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:35.701
-Yeah, I love Nashville!

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:37.634
Hi, Jemima.

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:40.267
Nashville, Tennessee.
Welcome to the show.

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:43.300
Jemima, what talent will you
be sharing with us tonight?

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.367
-I can open five beer bottles
in less than three seconds.

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.901
-Five -- In less than
three seconds?

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:51.868
Alright, now we're talking.
Here we go. That's a talent.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:53.467
Roots, can we get a drumroll,
please?

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:54.934
[ Drumroll ]

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:59.801
[ Bottles clanking ]

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:01.801
What?

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:04.200
Alright, whenever you're ready.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.400
Go.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.601
Whoa!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:12.200
♪♪

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.534
What?

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:14.934
Yo!

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:17.534
What?!

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:19.534
You are awesome!
What was --

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:20.801
That was unbelievable!

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:22.567
Can we see that again
in slow mo?

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:31.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
The accuracy. The accuracy.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:34.300
-I actually forgot
the sixth one.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.868
-Oh, come on!

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:38.133
That's how --
That's a mike drop.

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:39.801
That's a mike drop.

00:01:39.801 --> 00:01:41.033
Hey, you're awesome.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.400
Thank you for
that incredible talent.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.467
I appreciate you
being on the show.

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:45.267
Thank you very much.

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:47.601
That's cool, right?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:47.601 --> 00:01:49.400
Let's meet our next guest.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.167
Hello. What is your name
and where are you from?

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:54.667
-Hi, I'm Mark.
I'm from Toronto.

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:56.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:59.267
-We love -- Hi to everybody
in Toronto.

00:01:59.267 --> 00:02:01.133
Shout-out to Bloor Street.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:03.868
Hey, Mark, what is your talent

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:05.367
that you'll be showing us
tonight?

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:08.000
-My talent is I play
the clarinet and the piano

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.033
at the same time.
[ Audience murmurs ]

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.968
-And what song were you going
to be playing for us, Mark?

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:15.968
-I'm going to play
one of my own songs.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.334
-Yeah, perfect. I love it.

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:18.968
Whenever you're ready.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:30.467
♪♪

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:32.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:40.567
♪♪

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:43.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:46.467
-Yo, thank you very much
for that, Mark.

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:48.534
Do you have a title
for that song?

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.234
-"Happy Go Lucky."

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:52.801
-There you go.
That's my man right there.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:54.634
I appreciate you being
on the show, Mark.

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:56.367
That's a good talent.
Thank you very much.

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:58.400
Let's meet our final guest
right here.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.634
Oh, hey, guys.

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:02.200
What are your names
and where are you from?

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:05.501
-Hi, Jimmy. My name is Andie,
and this is my boyfriend Dylan.

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.534
-Hi, Dylan.
-We're from St. Louis, Missouri.

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:09.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Hey!

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.033
St. Louis!

00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:14.501
Shout-out to
Crown Candy Kitchen.

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:16.334
Thank you for being on the show.

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:18.968
What talent will you be
showing us tonight?

00:03:18.968 --> 00:03:22.534
-So, I'm pretty good at
catching shrimp in my mouth.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:24.934
And my boyfriend is going to be
my hibachi chef,

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:26.133
and he's going on throw them

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:28.434
and we're going to see
if I can catch them.

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:29.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:31.133
-Yep. Say it again.

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:33.734
So you're pretty good at
catching shrimp in your mouth?

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:36.534
And your boyfriend,
you're going to flip the shrimp?

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:38.701
Are you good at flipping shrimp?

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:40.934
-No.
-Okay. Alright, perfect.

00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:43.834
So you are -- you're going to
flip shrimp.

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:46.601
How did you learn that you have
this talent?

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:50.200
-Growing up, my family would
always love going to

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.133
get hibachi together,
and at a young age I learned

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:55.133
that this was one of
my secret, hidden talents.

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:56.801
And I warned him
when we started dating.

00:03:56.801 --> 00:04:00.100
[ Laughter ]
-To the dying end.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.133
-Well, alright.

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:02.734
You're going to go for it.

00:04:02.734 --> 00:04:05.234
See if you can catch
as many shrimp as you can.

00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:06.634
Drumroll please there, Quest.

00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:07.300
[ Drumroll ]

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:09.200
This is exciting.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.701
Alright.

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:11.734
-Okay.

00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:13.067
-Whenever you're ready.

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:16.300
Oh, my gosh. One.
♪♪

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.000
Oh, my God!

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.934
[ Laughter ]
Oh, my God!

00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:26.267
♪♪

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:28.467
Yeah, oh, my God!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:30.167
Hey, good job.

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:32.901
Very impressive.
Great job flipping, by the way.

00:04:32.901 --> 00:04:34.934
Oh, my God! Well done!

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:37.334
Well done! Very good.
Very talented.

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:39.300
That's all the time we have
for "Show Me Something Good."

